Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6afe: keep the handle of an LPASS core vote

The ADSP answers AFE_CMD_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST with the
vote's client handle, which the devote request has to send back. The
callback read that reply as a basic result (the handle as the status)
and q6afe_vote_lpass_core_hw() never filled in *client_handle, so every
devote went out with handle 0 and the ADSP refused it:

  qcom-q6afe aprsvc:service:4:4: cmd = 0x100f6 returned error = 0x1
  qcom-q6afe aprsvc:service:4:4: Unknown cmd 0x100f6

Each LPASS_HW_MACRO and LPASS_HW_DCODEC vote was then held for good,
and the ADSP kept LPASS up and never power collapsed once the codec
macros had probed. On a Retroid Pocket Flip 2 (SM8250) its qcom_stats
sleep count stopped as the macros bound and never moved again.

Store the handle from the reply and hand it to the caller, as the
downstream driver does, and don't report the devote's basic result as
an unknown command.

---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe.c
@@ -379,6 +379,7 @@
 	struct q6core_svc_api_info ainfo;
 	struct mutex lock;
 	struct aprv2_ibasic_rsp_result_t result;
+	uint32_t vote_handle;
 	wait_queue_head_t wait;
 	struct list_head port_list;
 	spinlock_t port_list_lock;
@@ -994,6 +995,8 @@
 				wake_up(&afe->wait);
 			}
 			break;
+		case AFE_CMD_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_DEVOTE_REQUEST:
+			break;
 		default:
 			dev_err(afe->dev, "Unknown cmd 0x%x\n",	res->opcode);
 			break;
@@ -1001,8 +1004,12 @@
 	}
 		break;
 	case AFE_CMD_RSP_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST:
+		/* The payload is the vote's client handle, not a status */
+		if (data->payload_size < sizeof(afe->vote_handle))
+			break;
+		afe->vote_handle = *(uint32_t *)data->payload;
 		afe->result.opcode = hdr->opcode;
-		afe->result.status = res->status;
+		afe->result.status = 0;
 		wake_up(&afe->wait);
 		break;
 	default:
@@ -1899,6 +1906,8 @@
 			       AFE_CMD_RSP_REMOTE_LPASS_CORE_HW_VOTE_REQUEST);
 	if (ret)
 		dev_err(afe->dev, "AFE failed to vote (%d)\n", hw_block_id);
+	else
+		*client_handle = afe->vote_handle;
 
 	return ret;
 }
